normal example: [2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2] k=3 -> buggy 9 | fixed 9 | brute 9 | ok
best window is the LAST one: [1, 2, 3] k=2 -> buggy 3 | fixed 5 | brute 5 | BUGGY WRONG
one element: [7] k=1 -> buggy 7 | fixed 7 | brute 7 | ok
k = n (one window): [4, -1, 2] k=3 -> buggy 5 | fixed 5 | brute 5 | ok
all negative: [-3, -1, -2] k=2 -> buggy -4 | fixed -3 | brute -3 | BUGGY WRONG
all equal: [5, 5, 5, 5] k=2 -> buggy 10 | fixed 10 | brute 10 | ok
